::: {.doc-subject}

Convert an event-time vector to a `Surv` response.
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/greenwood/blob/main/greenwood/_event_time.py#L869-L919){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-Kind.FUNCTION}
```python
as_surv(x)
```
:::

::: {.doc-text}

A port of etd's `as_surv()`. The type of the result depends on the status codes present,
ignoring missing elements:

- only `"e"` and `"r"`: a right-censored response, with status `1` for events.
- only `"e"` and `"l"`: a left-censored response, with status `1` for events.
- any other combination: an interval response, with R's codes `0` (right), `1` (exact), `2`
  (left), and `3` (interval).

Missing elements are missing in the result.
:::

## Parameters {.doc-parameters}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code>[x]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Any]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   An `EventTime` vector.
:::

## Returns {.doc-returns}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code> [Surv]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   The response.
:::

## Raises {.doc-raises}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code> [TypeError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   If `x` isn't an `EventTime` vector.
:::

## Examples {.doc-examples}

::: {#72274da9 .cell execution_count=1}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import greenwood as gw

x = gw.event_time(
    time=[7, 5, 3, 2],
    status=["e", "r", "l", "i"],
    time_max=[None, None, None, 4],
)
gw.as_surv(x).to_frame(format="polars")
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}
```{=html}
<div><style>
.dataframe > thead > tr,
.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
